.\" Manpage for ereport.
.TH man 1 "June 2026" "7.0" "ereport man page"
.SH NAME
ereport \- Produces a summary of the energy consumption reported by EAR's daemons.
.SH SYNOPSIS
ereport [options]

.SH DESCRIPTION
ereport is an administrator command that reports energy consumption data reported by EAR's daemons.

.SH OPTIONS
 
.nf
.ft CW
ereport --help
Usage: ereport [options]

Options:
  -h, --help                       Displays this message.
  -v, --version                    Displays the current EAR version.
  -b, --verbose                    Enables verbose mode for debugging purposes.

Filters:
  -s, --start-time <YYYY-MM-DD>    Sets the start of the period.
                                   Default: end time minus twice the insertion time.
  -e, --end-time <YYYY-MM-DD>      Sets the end of the period. Default: current time.
  -n, --nodes <node|all>           Filters by node name. Default: none.
  -u, --users <user|all>           Filters by username. Default: none.
  -G, --group <group|all>          Filters by group name. Default: none.
  -t, --etags <tag|all>            Filters by energy tag. Default: none.
  -i, --islands <eardbd|all>       Filters by EARDBD island. Default: none.

Output:
  -d, --expanded                   Expands island results to individual records.
                                   If no island is specified, prints all of them.
  -g, --global-energy              Shows EAR database global energy records.
                                   Defaults to the two previous EARGM T2 periods.
                                   This option can be modified with --start-time, but not --end-time.
  -x, --events                     Shows daemon events for the selected period.
  -z, --detailed                   Shows detailed periodic metrics for the selected period.
  -w, --total-savings              Shows the total energy savings in kWh.

.ft R
.fi


.SH Usage examples

The following example uses the 'all' nodes option to display information for each node, as well as a start_time so it will give the accumulated energy from that point moment until the current time.

[user@host EAR]$ ereport -n all -s 2018-09-18 
    Energy (J)       Node      Avg. Power (W)
    20668697         node1        146
    20305667         node2        144
    20435720         node3        145
    20050422         node4        142
    20384664         node5        144
    20432626         node6        145
    18029624         node7        128

This example filters by EARDBD host (one per island typically) instead:

[user@host EAR]$ ereport -s 2019-05-19 -i all
    Energy (J)        Node     
    9356791387        island1 
    30475201705       island2
    37814151095       island3 
    28573716711       island4 
    29700149501       island5 
    26342209716       island6

And to see the state of the custer's energy budget (set by the sysadmin) you can use the following:

[user@host EAR]$ ereport -g 
    Energy%  Warning lvl            Timestamp       INC th      p_state    ENERGY T1    ENERGY T2      TIME T1      TIME T2        LIMIT       POLICY
